<title>JAPAN: Alcatel Alsthom launches 5% yen/dlr samurai--Nikko.</title>
<headline>Alcatel Alsthom launches 5% yen/dlr samurai--Nikko.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/dollar dual currency samurai issue was announced by lead manager Nikko Securities on Wednesday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Alcatel Alsthom Cie Generale d'Electricite'</p>
<p> AMT		 20 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    5.0 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  27 Jan 2000</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  27 Jan 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Jan 13 to Jan 24</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA-, Moody's A1</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nikko Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi</p>
<p>NOTES: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive $8,697.92 for each 1.0 million-yen bond held at maturity.</p>
</text>
